  "relevance_note": "Single case report of a man with a diagnosis of LCAT deficiency: \"Our patient had a known diagnosis of LCAT deficiency.\"",
  "method_note": "Hand extraction of a short case report (no tables). One in-scope person, labelled 'patient' (rule 5). No LCAT variant, genetic test or zygosity is reported; the diagnosis was made 'after extensive studies including kidney biopsies', so the variants table is empty. Publication year is not printed in the converted text (left null). Kidney biopsy findings for this patient are not described, so renal histology checklist items are not reported. 'Significant coronary artery disease' was mapped to the checklist item 'atherosclerotic cardiovascular disease'; the paper does not use the word atherosclerotic for this patient. 'Findings on funduscopic examination were normal' is a whole examination; recorded as excluded 'abnormal findings on funduscopic examination' without narrowing it. Zoster-related pain and the absent rash are recorded as features although unrelated to LCAT deficiency per the authors. Background text on LCAT deficiency (anemia, proteinuria, hematuria) is general and was not applied to the patient. No contradictions found.",
